            ],
            "text_blocks": [
                {
                    "text": "Summary",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 277.98590087890625,
                        "y0": 69.93016052246094,
                        "x1": 347.2419738769531,
                        "y1": 97.64644622802734
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Introduction",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 92.10637664794922,
                        "x1": 117.33351135253906,
                        "y1": 108.73614501953125
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Scaling the number of parameters in a model, the amount of training data, or the computational budget has •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 125.67784118652344,
                        "x1": 529.5693359375,
                        "y1": 142.3076171875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "proven to be an effective yet simple technique for improving model performance.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 142.4635772705078,
                        "x1": 417.44573974609375,
                        "y1": 159.09335327148438
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "The feedforward (FFW) layers in standard transformer architectures, responsible for storing \"factual •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 159.24929809570312,
                        "x1": 510.51275634765625,
                        "y1": 175.8790740966797
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "knowledge\", incur a linear increase in computational costs and activation memory as the hidden layer width",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 176.03501892089844,
                        "x1": 532.3128662109375,
                        "y1": 192.664794921875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "grows.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 192.82078552246094,
                        "x1": 105.23429870605469,
                        "y1": 209.4505615234375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Mixture of Experts (MoE) has become a good alternative for decoupling the computational cost and the •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 209.60646057128906,
                        "x1": 520.0675048828125,
                        "y1": 226.23623657226562
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "parameter count.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 226.3922119140625,
                        "x1": 149.70333862304688,
                        "y1": 243.02198791503906
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Recent works have found that using more experts (high granularity) increases performance. When the •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 243.17799377441406,
                        "x1": 510.77618408203125,
                        "y1": 259.8077697753906
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "number of training tokens is compute-optimal, MoEs consistently outperform dense models in terms of",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 259.9636535644531,
                        "x1": 515.9345703125,
                        "y1": 276.5934143066406
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "FLOP efficiency.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 276.7494201660156,
                        "x1": 150.78378295898438,
                        "y1": 293.3791809082031
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Another reason to have many experts is lifelong learning. It has been proved that by simply adding new •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 293.5351867675781,
                        "x1": 513.7150268554688,
                        "y1": 310.1649475097656
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "experts and regularizing them properly, MoE models can adapt to continuous data streams.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 310.3208923339844,
                        "x1": 467.16571044921875,
                        "y1": 326.9506530761719
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Proposed Method",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 360.6780700683594,
                        "x1": 142.56295776367188,
                        "y1": 377.3078308105469
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Introduces the Parameter Efficient Expert Retrieval (PEER) layer, which is a MoE architecture using product",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 394.2496032714844,
                        "x1": 534.9534301757812,
                        "y1": 410.8793640136719
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "keys in the router and single-neuron MLPs as experts. A PEER layer consists of three components: a pool of",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 411.0352783203125,
                        "x1": 536.8397827148438,
                        "y1": 427.6650390625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "N experts E, a corresponding set of N product keys K, and a query network q. Here is how it works:",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 427.821044921875,
                        "x1": 488.8966369628906,
                        "y1": 444.4508056640625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Given a query x, retrieve a subset of k experts whose corresponding product keys have the highest inner •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 461.3924865722656,
                        "x1": 518.45556640625,
                        "y1": 478.0222473144531
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "products with the query q(x).",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 478.17822265625,
                        "x1": 196.84149169921875,
                        "y1": 494.8079833984375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Apply an activation function like sigmoid or softmax to obtain the router scores for these retrieved top k •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 494.9639892578125,
                        "x1": 518.8218994140625,
                        "y1": 511.59375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "experts.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 511.7496643066406,
                        "x1": 111.19815063476562,
                        "y1": 528.37939453125
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Compute the output by linearly combining the expert outputs weighted by the router scores. •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 528.535400390625,
                        "x1": 464.985595703125,
                        "y1": 545.1651611328125
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Product-Key Retrieval",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 562.1068115234375,
                        "x1": 164.43161010742188,
                        "y1": 578.736572265625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "If you have a large number of experts, each with a dimensionality d, then computing the top k indices can be •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 595.6784057617188,
                        "x1": 532.2140502929688,
                        "y1": 612.3081665039062
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "very expensive (O(Nd), N being >= 1e6 in this case).",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 612.4640502929688,
                        "x1": 297.4521179199219,
                        "y1": 629.0938110351562
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "The authors apply the product key retrieval technique used in the \"Large Memory Layers with Product Keys\" •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 65.72300720214844,
                        "y0": 629.2498168945312,
                        "x1": 536.0966186523438,
                        "y1": 645.8795776367188
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "paper. Instead of using N independent d-dimensional experts as keys, use two independent subsets, each",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 646.0355834960938,
                        "x1": 523.6098022460938,
                        "y1": 662.6653442382812
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "with dimensionality d/2, to form the keys.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 76.11661529541016,
                        "y0": 662.8212890625,
                        "x1": 254.92303466796875,
                        "y1": 679.4510498046875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                }
            ],
            "annotations": [],
            "visual_elements": [
                {
                    "type": "figure",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 0.0,
