        {
            "page_number": 11,
            "dimensions": [
                612.0,
                767.3587036132812
            ],
            "text_blocks": [
                {
                    "text": "Similarly, split the query vector q(x) into two sub-queries and then apply the top-k operation to the inner •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 77.85607147216797,
                        "x1": 522.470947265625,
                        "y1": 94.48583984375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "products between the sub-queries and sub-keys.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 80.96451568603516,
                        "y0": 94.64179992675781,
                        "x1": 287.26983642578125,
                        "y1": 111.27156829833984
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "This Cartesian product structure of K allows us to find the top k experts efficiently, reducing the complexity •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 111.42753601074219,
                        "x1": 540.193603515625,
                        "y1": 128.05731201171875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "from O(Nd) to O((√N + k^2) * d)",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 80.96451568603516,
                        "y0": 128.21327209472656,
                        "x1": 221.76930236816406,
                        "y1": 144.84304809570312
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "If you are thinking why this makes sense, consider doing napkin math by taking an example. Say,",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 161.7847137451172,
                        "x1": 485.1064147949219,
                        "y1": 178.41448974609375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "N=10000(which are your keys/experts K), d = 512 (dimensionality of query vector, and each key), and you",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 178.5704803466797,
                        "x1": 536.02685546875,
                        "y1": 195.20025634765625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "are searching for the top 10 values from the inner product of the query, and the keys.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 195.3561553955078,
                        "x1": 431.5902099609375,
                        "y1": 211.98593139648438
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Parameter Efficient Experts and Multi-Head Retrieval",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 413.57073974609375,
                        "x1": 306.6990966796875,
                        "y1": 430.20050048828125
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "In a PEER layer, every expert e is a hidden layer with a single neuron as shown below in equation 6. •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 447.1421813964844,
                        "x1": 507.4947509765625,
                        "y1": 463.7719421386719
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "This is different from the existing MoEs as the hidden layer is often set to the original size of the FFN layer. •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 463.92791748046875,
                        "x1": 539.2721557617188,
                        "y1": 480.55767822265625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "To adjust the reduced expressiveness in the PEER layer, the authors use multi-head retrieval, similar to the •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 480.71368408203125,
                        "x1": 535.2700805664062,
                        "y1": 497.34344482421875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "multi-head attention mechanism in transformers and the multi-head memory in PKMs.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 80.96451568603516,
                        "y0": 497.4993591308594,
                        "x1": 448.017333984375,
                        "y1": 514.1290893554688
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "h independent query networks instead of one, each computes its query and retrieves a separate set of k •",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 514.2850952148438,
                        "x1": 520.6036987304688,
                        "y1": 530.9148559570312
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "experts. However, different heads share the same pool of experts with the same set of product keys. The",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 80.96451568603516,
                        "y0": 531.0709228515625,
                        "x1": 525.2974243164062,
                        "y1": 547.70068359375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "outputs of these h heads are simply summed up. If one expert is retrieved (k = 1) per head, using a PEER",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 80.96451568603516,
                        "y0": 547.8565063476562,
                        "x1": 522.326416015625,
                        "y1": 564.4862670898438
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "layer with h heads is the same as using one expert with h hidden neurons.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 80.96451568603516,
                        "y0": 564.642333984375,
                        "x1": 390.33697509765625,
                        "y1": 581.2720947265625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "The million-dollar question: Why a large number of small experts?",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 614.99951171875,
                        "x1": 352.0406799316406,
                        "y1": 631.6292724609375
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "Look at the scaling law for MoE in equation 9 in the above figure where L is the final test loss, a, b, g, γ, α, β",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 631.7852783203125,
                        "x1": 527.7830810546875,
                        "y1": 648.4150390625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "are constants, D is the total number of training tokens, and the granularity G is the number of active experts.",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 70.57090759277344,
                        "y0": 648.5709838867188,
                        "x1": 533.1036376953125,
                        "y1": 665.2007446289062
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                }
            ],
            "annotations": [],
            "visual_elements": [
                {
