                    "vlm_description": "The figure presents mathematical notations and descriptions related to a research topic on \"Parameter Efficient Experts and Multi-Head Retrieval.\"\n\n1. **Equations:**\n   - Equation (6) defines `e_i(x)`, involving a sigma function and vectors.\n   - Equation (7) defines `f(x)` as a summation involving functions `f^i(x)` and `g_j(x)e_j(x)`.\n   - Equation (8) reformulates `f(x)` as another summation with vectors and a final product involving a matrix `W`.\n   - Equation (9) presents a function `L(P, D, G)` with parameters `g`, `a`, `b`, and terms involving `G_γ`, `P_α`, `D_β`.\n\n2. **Text Descriptions:**\n   - Details on query vectors `q(x)` and splitting them for computational efficiency.\n   - Context on reducing computational complexity by employing a Cartesian product structure.\n   - An example scenario with specified parameters for better understanding.\n   - Discussion on differences between PEER layers and existing Mixtures of Experts (MoEs).\n\n3. **Additional Points:**\n   - Discusses the use of multi-head attention and memory mechanisms in PEER layers.\n   - Highlights the independence and function of expert networks within this framework.\n\nThe equations and descriptions work together to explain the framework and mechanisms used in optimizing computational performance in expert models.",
                    "vlm_structured_data": null,
                    "associated_text_indices": null
                },
