        {
            "page_number": 12,
            "dimensions": [
                612.0,
                767.3587036132812
            ],
            "text_blocks": [
                {
                    "text": "G = P (active) / P (expert) where:",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 74.22307586669922,
                        "x1": 212.85675048828125,
                        "y1": 90.85284423828125
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "P = total number of parameters",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 91.00880432128906,
                        "x1": 203.860595703125,
                        "y1": 107.6385726928711
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "P(active) = number of active parameters per token",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 107.79454040527344,
                        "x1": 284.5928955078125,
                        "y1": 124.42430877685547
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "P (expert) = size of single expert",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 124.58027648925781,
                        "x1": 209.2845001220703,
                        "y1": 141.21005249023438
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "To improve model performance, we need to scale up P, D, and G. On the other hand, we need to limit P (active)",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 158.15171813964844,
                        "x1": 533.7090454101562,
                        "y1": 174.781494140625
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "because the computational and memory costs are primarily determined by the active parameters during",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 174.93748474121094,
                        "x1": 509.62591552734375,
                        "y1": 191.5672607421875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "training and inference. Now,",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 191.72315979003906,
                        "x1": 190.81192016601562,
                        "y1": 208.35293579101562
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "N = P / P (expert) = P * G / P (active)",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 225.294677734375,
                        "x1": 233.20376586914062,
                        "y1": 241.92445373535156
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "This implies that we should decrease the size of each expert, and increase the number of experts N. Also:",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 258.8661193847656,
                        "x1": 516.390625,
                        "y1": 275.4958801269531
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "P(expert) = (2*d_model + 1) * d_expert",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 292.4375915527344,
                        "x1": 237.64552307128906,
                        "y1": 309.0673522949219
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "P(active) = (2*d_model +1) * d_active; where",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 309.2233581542969,
                        "x1": 261.2935485839844,
                        "y1": 325.8531188964844
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "d_model = hidden dimension of the transformer",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 326.00909423828125,
                        "x1": 272.32379150390625,
                        "y1": 342.63885498046875
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "d_expert = number of hidden neurons used in one expert",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 342.7947692871094,
                        "x1": 311.2457275390625,
                        "y1": 359.4245300292969
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "d_active = total number of hidden neurons activated per token",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 359.5805358886719,
                        "x1": 334.52325439453125,
                        "y1": 376.2102966308594
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "For PEER, d_expert is 1, hence the granularity of PEER is always hk where h is the number of heads, and k is",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 393.1519775390625,
                        "x1": 536.0418090820312,
                        "y1": 409.78173828125
                    },
                    "layoutlm_embedding": null
                },
                {
                    "text": "the number of experts retrieved per head",
                    "bbox": {
                        "x0": 69.55802154541016,
                        "y0": 409.937744140625,
